=== SURVEY ===

Baseline route/page (must remain unchanged in off mode):
  - GET /api/v1/tire-pressure (internal/api/tire_pressure_handler.go) —
    deterministic snapshot reader using signal.StateReader.Timeline over
    tirePressureMappings projection ([VehicleStateTPMSPressureFrontLeft,
    FrontRight, RearLeft, RearRight]). Classifies each corner via fixed Pa
    thresholds (SOFT_LOW=200000, NORMAL_MIN=250000, NORMAL_MAX=350000,
    SOFT_HIGH=400000) → tire-pressure-trend-reasoning is layered AI on top
    of these same thresholds.
  - SPA: web/src/features/vehicle-systems/pages/TirePressurePage.tsx —
    consumes useTirePressureLatest() + useTirePressureRecent(); renders four
    corner panels with status badges, a deterministic threshold legend, and
    a warning banner when any corner is outside the normal band. The
    `normaliseTpmsToPa` band-aid (heterogeneous storage of Pa, kPa, psi,
    bar) lives client-side; the AI tool MUST mirror this exactly so model
    inputs match what the user sees on screen.

Routes / DTOs / hooks inspected:
  - /api/v1/tire-pressure → existing baseline (json:"summary","four_corners",
    "warnings"). Unchanged by this slice.
  - /api/v1/ai/tire-pressure/trends/explain (NEW) → POST {vehicle_id} →
    SSE narrative stream. Wrapped by ai.GuardedHandler so off-mode returns
    404 (proven below).

Registry entries inspected before edit:
