=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015, P1–P10, and the non-AI baseline:

1. ADR-015 §I1 (default-off):
   Registry entry sets DefaultOn=false. The frontend wrapper
   `withAiFeature('tire-pressure-trend-reasoning', …)` returns null
   unless ai_mode is non-off AND the per-feature toggle is true. The
   off-mode React test exercises ai_mode='off' AND ai_mode='cloud' +
   toggle=false to prove BOTH gates are required.

2. ADR-015 §I3 (baseline intact):
   Zero baseline files touched except TirePressurePage.tsx, where the
   only diff is one mounted component above the existing warning banner.
   The deterministic threshold panels, badges, refresh logic, range/
   pressure unit conversion, and warning banner all render unchanged
   when the AI gate is closed (proven by the third off-mode test case
   which exercises ai_mode='cloud' but toggle=false — baseline UI must
   still work).

3. ADR-015 §I4 (zero egress):
   Provider calls flow through the locked decorator chain (redaction →
   rate-limit → cost-cap → audit → trace) installed in F1–F5. The
   strategy registers PolicyTirePressureTrendReasoning (allow only
   ClassVehicleName, ModeRedactedTags) so VINs/locations/timestamps
   never reach the wire even with the gate open. Round-trip required
   per the slice prompt — the eval harness exercises this.

4. ADR-015 §I5 (hidden UI):
   The wrapper component is a true `null` return in off mode — there is
   no greyed-out "Coming soon" placeholder. Off-mode test asserts
   `queryByTestId('ai-feature-tire-pressure-trend-reasoning-root')` is
   null, not just hidden.

5. ADR-015 §I6 (404 routes):
   The Go handler is wrapped by ai.GuardedHandler in ai_routes.go. With
   ai_mode='off', the guard returns 404 for the registered POST route.
   `TestTirePressureReasoningAIOffShowsThresholdsOnly` exercises this
   directly via the in-process router and asserts status code 404 +
   absence of any AI body.

6. ADR-015 §I7 (per-feature toggle):
   Feature flag stored under settings.ai_features['tire-pressure-trend-
   reasoning']. The guard checks this discrete key (proven in F0/F2),
   so flipping unrelated AI features on must not enable this one. The
   off-mode React test's third case (`ai_mode='cloud'`, toggle=false)
   proves the per-feature gate independently.

7. ADR-015 §I10 (type system):
   Registry entry mirrored into web/src/ai/features.ts via aigen
   (`aigen --check` exit 0). AiFeatureId union now includes
   "tire-pressure-trend-reasoning". useAiEnabled / withAiFeature reject
   unknown IDs at compile time, eliminating drift between Go registry
   and TS callers.

8. ADR-015 §I12 (client-side resource isolation):
   Service worker chunk name `ai-tire-pressure-trend-reasoning`
   declared in registry; no jobs, push kinds, or storage keys added.
   Lazy-loaded code path is gated by the same wrapper, so off-mode
   bundles never request the chunk.

9. P10 baseline coexistence:
   No selection-by-flag inside business logic. The baseline page
   composes the AI wrapper at render time; the AI strategy is
   constructed in router.go alongside its sibling strategies. There is
   no `if ai_mode == off` branch anywhere in baseline code paths.

10. Forward-folded TimelineRow caveat:
    signal.StateReader.Timeline forward-folds projected fields, so
    every OutsideTemp emission re-emits the most recent TPMS values.
    Without consecutive-equal de-duplication in `extractCornerSeries`/
    `extractOutsideTempSummary` the per-corner sample size is inflated
    and the linear-regression slope drifts toward zero. The handler
    de-dupes consecutive identical values per corner before computing
    `linearSlopePaPerDay` — see the helper inline-comments. This
    matches the pattern used by drive-coaching's per-segment slope.

11. W1 inline wiring (P11/P12):
    The shipped SPA component imports `useAiStream` unconditionally at
    the top of the function body, points at the registered path
    `/ai/tire-pressure/trends/explain`, has a computed `disabled` prop
    (`!canGenerate`), and renders deltas inside an
    `AiOutputPanel` inside the gated wrapper. Zero placeholder strings
    (verified by the W1 inline scan). The on-mode test
    `TestTirePressureTrendReasoningAIOnWiredCallsRoute` asserts
    POST URL/body/headers, double-submit guard, and the `vehicleId
    missing → disabled` computed-disabled invariant.

